R[13]="Chose to **keep a row building's quads** through every designation change that keeps the `row` arrangement (only its back range and storeys change) over re-laying rows, because the quad is the plot's (shared party walls) and item 31's geometry floor protects built stock; a change to a `compound` arrangement keeps the quad byte-identical as the compound's frontage slot and adds the target's main structure behind it (V02 §3.9 W3b)."
