R[32]="Chose **M6 after M5 in three parts, the massing first** (with the roofscape) over the composer first, because the massing is on the first map and is what every view shows; V03's P0, P1 and P3 run on the base's buildings after M4 (J122) with `facadeBays` built at M3a-V2, and take the composer's rooms and dormer rows when M6b lands (V02 §8.1; V03 §8)."
R[35]="Chose a **slot-level size band** (`[p10, p90] × footprintShare ÷ count × buildingScale × sizeFactor`, the p10/p90 ratios **V11 §3.6.1's derivation ratios, mirrored as `sizeBandLo`/`sizeBandHi` (0.7 / 1.45, fixed)**, over 0.75 / 1.35), an **M3 least-footprint budget test** and an **M10 shrink that lowers the clamps and then falls down the reverse lattice**, over scaling alone, because the clamps undid the scale and T-V2-29 and T-V2-30 could not both pass; the **manor override** (prosperous 420 m², rich 650 m², plot 3 000 m², main share ≥ 0.6) for the owner's \"giant manor … bigger courts\" is V11's (V11 §3.6.1, J-V11.39), with M3's test the mechanism that removes a court family that cannot fit."
