R[58]="Chose to **design item 110's building parts in this volume** (V02 §2.6, §3.15–§3.17, §4.6, §5.6, §6.5, §7.7, §8.5), over leaving them to `volumes/_integrate`, because this volume holds the composer's context and V03, V05, V09, V10 and V11 build on its tier record and deck row."
R[61]="Chose **stairs as solid `shed`-roofed wings laid on the terrace below**, the stair side's inset deepened to hold the run, over stairs cut into the upper tier or projecting through the step, because every tier then stays a simple nested ring and every stair is contained in what it stands on; both the stepped pyramid's great axial stair and the terraced palace's flights along the faces are reached. **Its cost is recorded:** with each front terrace holding a whole flight, the summit stands `(Σ f_k − (n − 1)d) ÷ 2` behind tier 0's centre — 2.4 / 3.6 / 3.3 / 4.4 m on the stepped temple's median stacks at its grade 1.0–1.2 (6.4 m at grade 0.9; the receipt, V02 §3.10.3) — accepted as the price of nested rings and contained stairs, the steeper stair (as the stepped temples of the Americas were climbed) bringing it down, and shown to the owner's panel (V02 §7.5 (3)), which may veto it toward stairs cut into the tiers."
R[68]="Chose **no basement, crypt or dig on any deck, a mole included**, over a masonry-mole exception, because the deck is not ground; an `always`-crypt class is never a deck class (V11's load check), so the no-refusal crypt ladder never meets a deck. The gate reads **the use, not only the class**: a use to which a dossier crypt record binds is never placed on a deck either (`deckOk` per use; a hand placement bends landward; a mutation relocates the use), because the dossier is the sole immutable truth (items 20, 22) and a bridge chapel may carry a recorded crypt. **A quay built on the bank is ground**, not a deck (the terrain datum, the ordinary basement gate, a dig floor), so \"the deck is not ground\" covers moles, piers, bridge decks and quays built out over water."
