R[72]="Chose to **add no building-side retaining-wall rule** — the massing reads only `H` and the levelled datum — over a wall setback or a wall-hugging range in the massing, because S10 and S11's levelling and the site plan own where a wall runs (item 110 (a)); the rear setback may be 0 (a row built against the terrace wall), and **the datum reads the building's own terrace** — a sample within `terrace.wallBandCm` of a wall is taken on the centroid's side (item 231) — because a sample on or across the wall's line would read the platform across the wall, floating the house toward the terrace above or sinking it toward the one below; every datum sample is `levelledGroundCm` (J-V2.98), the terrace V01's `stepProfile` reads on each side of the wall."
