R[79]="Chose **a named bend for every structural limit of V02's edits** — the sealed stair form `none`; ground wings beside a stack; a block beside it as a range; `tiers` on a non-stepped building as `family: 'stepped'` first; `internal` over a solid base as `none` (all solid) or `axial`; `single` for `family: 'stepped'` on a deck; the building's removal for its last wing (and for tier 0 with nothing beside it); the party-wall line's move for a row quad's reshape and a gap for its removal; a too-small wing grown; an op beyond the plot clipped with `join` offered; an unreachable family as the nearest reachable one; a gate hall with no gate range as a gate passage; a room with no admitting host moved to one — over refusals with offers, because item 101 R2 lets a tool refuse only what item 20 forbids and what a lock protects. `none` is lawful wherever tier 0 is solid, not only where every tier is (a sealed stack's unreached shrine is the same case, and it gives removing a stair a lawful bend on a platform under storeyed tiers); removing a row quad that is not the last wing leaves a gap rather than moving a plot line (the nearest form of a removal is a removal)."
R[83]="Chose **the stair's foot as a solid stack's main entrance, with the plan rooted at the first landing door** (and no plan above the ground for a building with no storeyed wing, its basement and access heads still planned; a sealed stack with a storeyed shrine keeps the shrine's plan, unreached), over a main door on the shrine, because *Entrances* rule 1 puts the main entrance on the footprint and a solid stack has no storey there (item 230)."
R[84]="Chose **an elliptical two-ring `ovalCourt` family** — an arcaded façade ring and a solid seating ring round an open floor, gate passages at the major-axis ends — over the court-institution's rectangles or the fantasy `regularCourt`, because the amphitheatre is a historical form the owner's second fixture names and the solid wings already carry seating; shipped as `massOval` in `@plat/plots` from M3a (the fixture stands there), with an `arena` row that fills its precinct (`claimShare` .5–.8) and a volume-11 plot override (X27). The floor's bar is at least 10 % of the hull, over 35 %, because the historical amphitheatres' arenas are about 13–20 % of their hulls (the largest ≈ 13.5 %), so 35 % would forbid the real form."
