R[103]="Chose (a) to keep `sizeBandLo`/`sizeBandHi` in `composition.json`'s constants as **fixed mirrors** of V11 §3.6.1's derivation ratios (`own`, a `fixed:` note, no register entry — the one constant of V02 §3.10.9's table that is not calibratable) over dropping them and reading V11's compiler constants, because M10 applies the ratios at run time to a compiled row whose authored p10 = p50 = p90 while V11 holds them only in its compiler, and a mirror marked fixed can neither drift by a calibration nor leave M10 without a value; and (b) to bring **item 426 and item 224 to M3a whole** with item 229 — both `composition?` fields, the `heights` comment and the hint clause — over splitting each into an M3a part and an M6 part, because no part changes a base behaviour before a writer or a hint exists (V11's C3b replacement and the base outline builder's stepped and oval constructions are the first, both at M3a)."
R[104]="Chose (a) to **ship the `PorchKindRow`s with M3a-V2's `composition.json`** (data only; the porch itself is composed from M6b) over V01 holding porch sizes of its own until M6a, because the rows are five authored data rows with no build effort, a second copy of their sizes in V01's constants would state this volume's facts twice, and a reserve sized from the real rows from M5 leaves the hood pins where they are when the composer's porches appear at M6b (J-V1.75's order-independence); and (b) to **build item 303's hole sentence alone at M3a**, with item 229, over the whole item at M3a or leaving the arena floor to its template's yard row until M6, because `massOval`'s arena is laid from M3a and three bars (T-V2-42, T-V1-26, T-V1-54) read its floor as a `court` before M6, while the item's other sentences have no reader before M6. A base template's hole whose kind the yard rows set otherwise before M3a is retyped once at M3a, a declared shift (§13.3), over keeping template-typed holes, because two typings of one kind of place would split every reader of the court."
R[105]="Chose (a) that **a storey-less stack against a retaining wall roots its basement at V03's `basementDoor(b)`** and a storey-less temple's crypt is planned (X18; item 371 (c)'s step-5 root clause), over rooting it at a tomb door the plan never opens; (b) to **home the whole derived-at-read block of V02 §2.6 in `@plat/plots` at M3a-V2** — `rebaseStack` and `stairTreads` with the four stack helpers — over naming only the four, because `rebaseStack` runs on the base's re-basing paths from M3a and `@plat/buildings` depends on `@plat/plots`, so no function of the block can live above V03's eager readers (`ground(b)`, `floorCm`, `basementDoor(b)`); (c) to write every bar registration's `preset` as `'default'` (V12 §2.1's `PresetArm`) over leaving the field to the registering seat, because none of V02's eleven bars generates its towns under a parity preset — T-V2-37's preset clause reads the compiled cell, not a town, and the `FM` measurements are V12's `reference` run, not a bar."
