R[107]="Chose to **state stair 0's approach strip once, in V02 §4.6's ground-wing bullet**, with its own V02 §1b row pointing there and `landingM`'s constants row naming it among its consumers, over moving the definition into V02 §3.15.1's construction, because V03's two door functions cite the strip as V02 §4.6 bounds it and no step of the construction lays or stores it (ST2–ST7 place the reserve and the stairs; the strip only bounds what may stand in front of stair 0)."
R[108]="Chose to **key the raised lift and the crypt-only half raise on the ground wings over the basement's ring**, over the crypt's seed wings, because V03 derives basements under other wings — the ground wings' whole inset of a crypt no stair reaches (V03 §3.7.4), an author's crypt ring on a building without a basement (V03 §4.2) and the far-third seed where `cryptSeedWings(b)` returns none — and under the seed-wing key each of those put storey −1 into an unraised or unlifted storey 0. A derived crypt stays under its seed wings on the `half` and `raised` rungs (V03 §3.7.4 step 2), so J-V2.91's raised choir over a half-sunk crypt is unchanged; a solid tier 0 holding the crypt inside it keeps its height. No declared shift: the crypt parts are M6-U's, unbuilt."
